+      <ol type="1" spacing="normal" indent="adaptive" start="1" pn="section-1-3">
+        <li pn="section-1-3.1" derivedCounter="1.">This specification reserves one Ethernet unicast address,
+00-00-5E-00-52-13, for use with Proxy Mobile IPv6.  This reserved
+link-layer address <bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14> be used by the mobile access gateway in
+a Proxy Mobile IPv6 domain, on all of the access links that it
+shares with the mobile nodes.  The protocol configuration
+variable FixedMAGLinkLayerAddressOnAllAccessLinks <xref target="RFC5213" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5213"/>
+<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14> be set to this reserved address.  The mobile access
+gateway can use this address in all packet communication with the
+mobile node on the access links.  Considerations from <xref target="RFC5342" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5342"/>
+apply with respect to the use of Ethernet parameters in IETF
+protocols.  This address is allocated from the registry &quot;IANA
+Ethernet Address Block - Unicast Use&quot;.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.2" derivedCounter="2.">This specification reserves an IPv6 interface identifier,
